# The product of two balls with 2-limb centers: the center by mul_2_2, and the radius from upper
# bounds of the center magnitudes, plus U |cz| + V from the claims of mul_2_2.
kernel:        ball_mul_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
input:         cy = cy0 cy1
input:         stored ry
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
value:         cx*cy
requires:      normalized cx
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      normalized cy
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       normalized cz
ensures:       encloses cz rz x*y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 4
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_mul_2_correct
source:        midpoint-radius product (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

(cz0, cz1) = mul_2_2(cx0, cx1, cy0, cy1)
ax         = abs_upper_2(cx0, cx1)
ay         = abs_upper_2(cy0, cy1)
t1         = rmul(ax, ry)
t2         = rmul(ay, rx)
t3         = rmul(rx, ry)
s1         = radd(t1, t2)
s2         = radd(s1, t3)
mz         = abs_upper_2(cz0, cz1)
d0         = rmul(const unit_computed(mul_2_2), mz)
d          = radd(d0, const tiny_computed(mul_2_2))
rz         = radd(s2, d)
